    "title": "Progressive Group Targets Senators Over Judicial Nominee Votes",
    "text": "• Demand Justice, a progressive group, is launching a $1 million advertising campaign targeting Senators John Fetterman (D-PA), Maggie Hassan (D-NH), and Angus King (I-ME).\n• The campaign, which began Wednesday, focuses on senators who voted to confirm some of President Donald Trump's judicial nominees.\n• The group's president, Josh Orton, stated this is an initial effort and threatened further action against lawmakers if they don't take a stronger stance against Trump.\n• The campaign is in response to eight Senate Democrats, including Fetterman, Hassan, and King, joining Republicans to end a government shutdown.\n• Orton stated that Democrats should not give bipartisan cover to judges who avoid acknowledging Trump's 2020 election loss or the January 6th Capitol attack.\n• Trump's judicial nominees have also drawn criticism for their views on abortion, with roughly half having revealed anti-abortion views.\n• Fetterman defended his voting record, stating he votes with Democrats over 90% of the time.\n• Hassan said she voted to reopen the government because of constituent suffering and the unlikelihood of a better deal.\n• King admitted his vote to confirm a federal judge in Missouri was a mistake.",
